language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_053_graceful_graphs: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A labelling f of the nodes of a graph with q edges is graceful if f assigns each node a unique label from {0, 1, ..., q}, and when each edge xy is labelled with |f(x) - f(y)|, the edge labels are all different. Find a graceful labelling of the given graph.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_053_graceful_graphs.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_053_graceful_graphs.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_053_graceful_graphs_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_053_graceful_graphs.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_053_graceful_graphs_1.param -run-solver

$ n: number of nodes
given n : int(1..)
$ m: number of edges (the q of the problem)
given m : int(1..)
$ graph[e,1] and graph[e,2]: the two end nodes of edge e, numbered from 0 (the data's index 0 is node 0; the model's node k is the data's node k-1, so the nodes are 0-based as in the data)
given graph : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..2)] of int(0..n-1)

$ nodes[k]: the label of node k-1 (the data's node numbering), a label from 0 to m; indices 1-based, so nodes[k] is the data's node k-1
find nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..m)
$ edges[e]: the label of edge e, the difference of the labels of its two end nodes (indices 1-based, in the order of graph)
find edges : matrix indexed by [int(1..m)] of int(1..m)

branching on [nodes]
such that
$ each node has a different label
allDiff(nodes),
$ each edge is labelled with the absolute difference of the labels of its two end nodes
forAll e : int(1..m) . (edges[e] = |nodes[graph[e,1] + 1] - nodes[graph[e,2] + 1]|),
$ the edge labels are all different
allDiff(edges)
